                                            "XebtF": {
                                              "content": "Robin, the Gmail hook reported an error, but both builds processed successfully. I checked both hook logs: the last rg search found no matching wording in the triage rules and returned exit code 1. OpenClaw surfaced that as “Bash failed”.\n\nBoth runs continued after those errors, archived the notices under 98 Otterware, and verified the filing. Nothing needs retrying.\n\nThe fix is in the triage step, not Gmail delivery: skip daily note files that don’t exist yet, treat rg exit code 1 as “no matches,” and keep alerting on real errors."
                                            }
